  title "Aurora Wept Through Breathing Wounds"
  summary "This surreal chronicle depicts a catastrophic conflict in a frozen sea realm involving orcas, shamans, and mystical forces. Gork Slaughterend and other orca warriors, bearing inherited wounds from battles with entities like the penguin Netemia, engage in a devastating siege against Light Ingjeizhi spire and the Aurora Stack. Shamans perform a forbidden ritual invoking a dead god's power, speaking the spell \"Pod-bond Annihilation\" that collapses pod-law and causes mutual destruction—orcas and shamans alike bleed, tunnels collapse, and the spire becomes corrupted. The chronicle ends with the frozen sea settling into an eternal, inexpressible hunger, carrying the weight of all those who bled into its ice, with the wound and its legacy persisting across generations."
